        },
        "valueString": "Heart sounds dual; no murmur."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Brief mental state examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Cooperative; speech normal rate and volume; affect mildly anxious and reactive; thought process coherent; thought content appropriate; no psychosis; no suicidal ideation expressed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Work-related stress and sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Works full time as a marketing coordinator and is working long hours on a major campaign. Reports high work stress and conflict with manager over the last 2–3 months, feeling 'constantly on edge' and unable to switch off. Sleep-onset insomnia with rumination about work. Appetite okay."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and anxiety symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Describes mood as 'stressed and a bit overwhelmed.' Denies persistent low mood, anhedonia, hopelessness, and suicidal ideation. No current panic attacks. Often feels jittery with palpitations when stressed."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Alcohol use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Drinks about 2–3 glasses of wine most nights, up to 1 bottle on weekends; says it 'helps me relax.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cannabis and other substance use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Vapes cannabis a couple of nights per week for sleep. Denies other illicit drugs. Patient was receptive to discussion that alcohol and cannabis can worsen anxiety and sleep, but was defensive and said they are the 'only thing that works.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-18",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Additional concerns reported"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Raised shoulder pain, a mole on the back, period pain, palpitations, an unusual taste, sleep problems, a request to check iron, and a toenail change. These concerns were not assessed in detail at this visit."
      }
    },
